# Build the lightweight `src/user` exporter and cross-platform GUI

Create the end-user Python surface under `src/user/`. It validates a lawful
installed game in place, asks for target platforms, runs public-safe
reconstruction/build procedures, and writes only to its own extracted release
workspace and `dist/`; it never writes into the original game installation.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Support CPython 3.12+ for the public user tool independently of the
  exact repository-development Python pin.
- [ ] Ship `shar.py`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `NOTICES.md`, `game.jsonl`, `dist.json`,
  `code/*.py`, `scripts/*`, `mods/`, and reviewed public
  `algorithms/**/algorithm/*.txt` plans from `src/user/`; never ship authoring
  `in/`, `master/`, or `out/` payloads.
- [ ] Keep helper Python modules under `code/` and keep executable/script
  construction entry code at the end of the owning `.py` file.
- [ ] Provide `scripts/windows/shar.ps1` and
  `scripts/macos-linux/shar.sh` launch helpers.
- [ ] Provide a lightweight GUI for selecting/dragging/pasting the original game
  path and selecting any supported target without auto-selecting the host.
- [ ] Discover required algorithm evidence by relative path under the selected
  lawful source/search roots. Offer only targets and optional mod inputs that
  the user actually possesses.
- [ ] Present available language overlays individually and offer the Muckluck
  compatibility mod only when its required local source evidence is present.
- [ ] Save choices in release-local `user.json`, with all target toggles on by
  default until the user disables them.
- [ ] Never modify, overwrite, patch, or clean the original installed-game path.
- [ ] Show progress/ETA without claiming resumability until resumable state is
  actually implemented.
- [ ] Keep `CHANGELOG.md` handwritten and player/modder-facing; do not generate
  it from commits, compiler output, or technical build logs.
- [ ] Update README command names, file tree, and platform instructions whenever
  the release contract changes.

## Dependencies

Depends on stable source validation, algorithms, and package-layout contracts.

## Evidence

`src/user/README.md` and its boundary sidecar now establish the source-domain
authority for the future lightweight release surface without claiming that any
exporter, GUI, launcher, or release payload has been implemented yet.

This is the intended lightweight path for ordinary players; from-scratch Unreal
repository builds remain an expert/developer workflow.
